comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-13T21:59:48.347Z",codex-root,"Duplicate check 2026-07-13: prior audits captured point-in-time state but no open execution task owns the typed graph baseline,isolate classification,waiver ledger,and body-to-edge drift required by pm-a8zm."
  "2026-08-03T11:22:46.046Z","harness:codex","All-status baseline evidence 2026-08-03 after organization: 2,296 current items and 43,816 immutable events; statuses are 337 open, one in progress, 1,944 closed, and 14 canceled. All 338 active items have acceptance criteria, estimates, risk, confidence, and dependencies; pm-doxj is the sole unparented active item and is the intentional portfolio root. Storage integrity parsed all 2,296 items and 2,310 history streams with zero missing or unreadable streams, hash mismatches, chain mismatches, merge conflicts, repair reconciliations, or runtime-cache leakage. Graph profile is 2,299 nodes including three classified terminal-only missing endpoints, 10,761 deduplicated directed edges, one component, zero active isolates, zero active degree-one nodes, ten layers, and a nine-edge critical path. Graph audit is back at the pre-change baseline of eleven informational legacy findings only: one legacy duplicate class, one no-blocker sentinel class, eight terminal ordering-cycle classes, and one terminal missing-reference class. Active lifecycle has zero terminal parents, stale blockers, dependency cycles, or parent cycles. A 0.90 all-status duplicate scan returns fifteen known historical or false-positive clusters and none contains the three new items. Strict historical debt remains explicit: 295 terminal resolution backfills, broad legacy reviewer or sprint fields, 195 missing linked paths and 21 tracked orphan candidates owned by pm-e9zh and pm-j8z6; no placeholder normalization, pruning, or terminal mutation was applied. Command census: 76 canonical commands, 159 runtime paths, 2,096 flags, 31 placeholder intents, and 21 missing default token budgets. Provenance census: model 0, effort 702, role 37, topic 0. Verification passed three linked gates including 78 release-automation tests, build, and the 11-gate registry across 45 enforced pipelines; published 2026.8.3 passed npm, npx, bunx, MCP, bin, negative-control, and GitHub Release checks with exactly one daily release."
  "2026-08-04T05:52:11.793Z","harness:claude-code","Reproducible all-status graph census, 2026-08-04, taken directly from the tracked item files rather than from a graph command, so it is independent of read-time canonicalization and of the active-node scoping that pm-6olc95 owns.\n\nMethod. Parse every file under the per-type storage folders, both TOON dependency encodings, the tabular header form and the expanded list form. Reading only one encoding undercounts badly: the expanded form alone yields 855 rows and reads as a nearly edgeless corpus. Both forms together yield 9,152 rows across 2,301 items.\n\nAuthored edge totals by kind: related 5,512; implements 2,206; discovered_from 330; blocked_by 277; parent 275; blocks 241; verifies 200; supersedes 57; related_to 43; child 8; incident_from 3.\n\nTimestamp coverage is 9,152 of 9,152, exactly 100 percent, with no kind and no month missing. Author coverage is 7,788 of 9,152, 85.1 percent, leaving 1,364 rows whose asserting identity is unrecoverable. Distribution by creation month is 2026-02 84, 2026-03 147, 2026-04 238, 2026-05 91, 2026-06 265, 2026-07 7,863, 2026-08 464. Eighty-six percent of the graph was authored in one month, which is the backfill, and it is the reason a HEAD-only reading overstates historical connectedness.\n\nConnectivity by status, counting an edge as discriminating when its kind is not part of the hierarchy spine of parent, child, and implements:\n\nOpen, 331 items. Zero have no discriminating edge. Median total degree 11, median discriminating degree 10. The active frontier is saturated and needs no enrichment.\n\nClosed, 1,956 items. 257 have no discriminating edge at all and participate solely through the hierarchy spine; by type they are Task 122, Issue 51, Feature 46, Chore 30, Story 6, Decision 2. A further set brings the total with at most one distinct discriminating kind to 1,364, which is 69.7 percent. Median total degree 4, median discriminating degree 3.\n\nCanceled, 14 items. Zero have no discriminating edge. Median total degree 5.\n\nReading. The enrichment frontier is entirely inside terminal history, exactly where this plan already sequences it last and where pm-a8zm requires dedicated changelog-safe batches coordinated with pm-e9zh. The 257 spine-only closed items are the natural first wave boundary and the 1,364 at-most-one-kind set is the second. No edge was written to any closed item to produce this census, and none should be written outside those batches.\n\nTwo vocabulary observations that belong in the waiver ledger rather than in remediation. The related_to rows, 43 of them, are the alias population pm-4020c5 owns and are still being minted at HEAD. The blocks rows, 241 of them, are unmirrored without exception: not one has a reciprocal blocked_by on its target, which is the correct state under the current model and simultaneously the reason pm-jkbqt8 reports them unreachable to the scheduler. Both populations have grown since their owning items measured them, which is the general gap now filed as pm-ips23h."
